      <h3>Why isolation matters here</h3>
      <p>Legacy and modern implementations often disagree on things that have nothing to do with business logic — timezone handling in the host environment, a globally installed package version, leftover module-level state from a previous run. Running both in fresh, isolated Docker containers per input batch removes that entire class of false positives and false negatives before the diff engine ever sees a result.</p>
